The following tear effects when generated by Fruit Cake work differently than that of the base item:
* {{i|Eye of Greed}}: Isaac will not lose coins from this effect occurring.
* {{i|Ipecac}}: There is no associated damage up/poison effect/arcing.
* {{i|My Reflection}}: There is no associated shot speed up.
* {{i|Polyphemus}}: Only the ability to pierce enemies on overkill damage is applied; there is no associated damage bonus with the tear.
* {{i|Proptosis|nr}} : There is no associated damage multiplier, effectively decreasing damage dealt.
* {{i|Tiny Planet}}: There is no associated range up.

{{dlc|r}} The unique tear effects available to some [[wisps]] made by {{i|Book of Virtues|n}} can also be used by Fruit Cake. This can include:
* Drop hearts/coins/[[cards]]/[[runes]] on kill. The tear must deal the final hit; earlier hits do not flag enemies to drop the consumable on death.
* Teleport enemies to a random location in the room. This cannot affect [[Bosses]].
* Transform enemies into {{e|Poop}} (similarly to {{i|E. Coli}}).
* Transform enemies into random wisps.

Tear effects used in the pool of Fruit Cake do not need their base items unlocked in order to be used. This means that Fruit Cake can occasionally give previews of synergies that are locked.

